@@ -765,6 +771,26 @@ c.tool_offset(toolno, z_offset,  x_offset, diameter, frontangle, backangle, orie
 `set_optional_stop(int)`::
   set optional stop on/off
 
+`set_joint_availability(int, int)`::
+  Request availability for one joint. The first argument is the joint number;
+  the second is zero to release it or non-zero to acquire it. The command must
+  be issued at an idle execution boundary. Use `wait_complete()` to wait for
+  the hardware acknowledgement and the complete transition.
+
+`set_spindle_availability(int, int)`::
+  Request availability for one spindle. The first argument is the spindle
+  number; the second is zero to release it or non-zero to acquire it. The
+  command must be issued at an idle execution boundary. Use `wait_complete()`
+  to wait for the complete transition.
+
+Joint and spindle dictionaries also expose `availability_state` and
+`availability_fault`. State values match the motion HAL pins: 0 disabled,
+1 enabling, 2 homing, 3 available, 4 disabling, 5 fault. A nonzero fault code
+reports a failed transition; see the motion HAL pin documentation. A command's
+completion includes nonvolatile position validation, required homing, or release cleanup,
+not just a hardware ACK edge. Acquisition requires Machine On; release and fault
+recovery are also permitted while off. These commands need no M-code interface.
+
 `set_spindle_override(int [, int])`::
   set spindle override enabled. Defaults to spindle 0.
 
