new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e1bde10
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/runtime-availability-regressions/README
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+Production-path availability regressions. Each case starts LinuxCNC with POSIX
+simulation and uses its NML command/status channels and real HAL servo thread.
+The amplifier and homing latches run after motion-controller every servo cycle.
+Select individual cases with AVAILABILITY_REGRESSION_CASES for mutation checks.
+The extra-joint case verifies configuration rejection before Machine On because
+no external posthome command ownership/completion contract is supported.
+The fault case records EMC_ABORT_MOTION_OR_IO_RCS_ERROR through the standard
+ON_ABORT_COMMAND hook, distinguishing error handling from a machine-off abort
+without polling transient status. The sequence case verifies that an
+availability-controlled joint cannot define a Home All sequence.
+
+INI fixtures are generated by test.sh from the shared FIXTURE.BASE and local
+*.ini.in overrides. Run python3 ../runtime-availability/make-fixtures.py before
+launching an individual case directly. @unset explicitly removes an inherited
+key. Generated INIs are ignored; edit the base or the case override instead.
+Handoff regressions cover abort during a spindle index wait followed by release
+and reacquisition (including a fresh encoder handshake), X/Z/C Machine Off/On
+while released C feedback moves externally, and JOG_STOP during acknowledgment
+and volatile acquisition homing waits. Released motion state remains frozen
+while the raw HAL feedback pin stays live.
